v0.4.5
======

Date: November 26, 2025

    * Implemented netfileops for easy file sharing between mesh nodes.
    * Introducing iosk standard distribution and workspace overlay.
    * Add "-4" option to `ask` for gemini-3-pro-preview / gpt-5.1.
    * Improved `ask` command prompt construction for caching.


v0.4.4
======

Date: November 21, 2025

    * User context inspector aka glassbox.
    * Notifications aka sentinel.
    * New "Columns" view for IOSK File Explorer.
    * SKYBOARD.
    * Refactored frontend and backend.
    * Misc. improvements.


v0.4.3
======

Date: November 13, 2025

    * Windows can be grouped together as tabs.
    * Improvements to chat including color and private messages in the web UI.
    * Add a Web Browser window.
    * Misc. windowing and other improvements.


v0.4.2
======

Date: November 7, 2025

    * Introducing the web frontend: SideKick Wins!
    * Improvements to the `ask` command: added '-w' (--work) option.
    * Other misc. fixes and improvements.


v0.4.1
======

Date: October 29, 2025

    * Lots of fixes and improvements to meshing.
    * Add a selection of ollama models.
    * Path fixes for running directly on Windows.
    * Parser fixes for quoted strings and command substitution.
    * Make sure logout actually happens for `exit` and `logout`.
    * Improvements to key handling for shutdown / headless mode.
    * Remove `whatami` command; add '-d' option to `whoami` to get device.
    * Add `uptime` command.


v0.4.0
======

Date: October 9, 2025

    * Mesh networking support with rooms (aka netroom).
    * New room commands: `room`, `rooms`, `clroom`, `topic`.
    * New general commands: `hostname`, `login`, `logout`.
    * New network commands: `port`, `mesh`, `unmesh`, `on`, `where`, `whereami`.
    * Add a `watch` command.
    * Improved shell parser doesn't need spaces around pipe, redirection, etc.
    * Modified startup now always logs in as root.


v0.3.6
======

Date: October 7, 2025

    * Automated token-rate limiting (1 million tokens per model per minute).
    * Process management and new `ps`, `top`, and `kill` commands.
    * Add `trace` command for prompt debugging.
    * Add a `sleep` command, interruptible by direct message or `kill`.
    * Add a `reset` command to start over.
    * Added --openai option to the regular sidekick `ask` command.
    * More proposals and documentation updates.


v0.3.5
======

Date: October 4, 2025

    * Send direct messages with `@user` or `send -u user`
    * Can now `pause` and `unpause` the agents.
    * Add `reattach` for changing devices and `whatami` to find out.
    * Add the `who` and `ver` commands.
    * Shell parser now recognizes end-of-line comments.
    * A proposal for adjustable agent timing.


v0.3.4
======

Date: October 2, 2025

    * Add `send` command for sending file contents in the chat.
    * Better handling of markdown blocks.
    * Updated `date` command accepts a format string.
    * Fix to command-line parsing -p option in `ask`.
    * Cumulative token counts in `tokens` output.
    * Updated `ticket` command to include more details.
    * Misc. tweaks and cleanup.


